["<aside class=\"callout warn\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law. Synopsis 2026 to 2028, edition dated 2 October 2026.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 352\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"What a .22 rimfire may legally hunt in BC, from the methods table on page 13 of the synopsis: grouse and ptarmigan yes, wild turkey yes (note 2: grouse, ptarmigan or turkey only among birds), snowshoe hare yes, coyote, raccoon and skunk yes. Quail and pheasant no, ducks and geese no, deer, bear, elk and moose no.\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"352\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"27\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">What the .22 may hunt in BC</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Rimfire (.22) in the page 13 methods table:</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"70\" width=\"372\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"91\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Grouse, ptarmigan</text><rect x=\"270\" y=\"75\" width=\"52\" height=\"20\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"296\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">Yes</text><text x=\"332\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">note 2</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"106\" width=\"372\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"127\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Wild turkey</text><rect x=\"270\" y=\"111\" width=\"52\" height=\"20\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"296\" y=\"126\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">Yes</text><text x=\"332\" y=\"126\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">note 2</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"142\" width=\"372\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"163\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Snowshoe hare</text><rect x=\"270\" y=\"147\" width=\"52\" height=\"20\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"296\" y=\"162\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">Yes</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"178\" width=\"372\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"199\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Coyote, raccoon, skunk</text><rect x=\"270\" y=\"183\" width=\"52\" height=\"20\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"296\" y=\"198\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">Yes</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"214\" width=\"372\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"235\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Quail, pheasant</text><rect x=\"270\" y=\"219\" width=\"52\" height=\"20\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#FF6A13\"/><text x=\"296\" y=\"234\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">No</text><text x=\"332\" y=\"234\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">note 2</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"250\" width=\"372\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"271\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Ducks, geese</text><rect x=\"270\" y=\"255\" width=\"52\" height=\"20\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#FF6A13\"/><text x=\"296\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">No</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"286\" width=\"372\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"307\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Deer, bear, elk, moose</text><rect x=\"270\" y=\"291\" width=\"52\" height=\"20\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#FF6A13\"/><text x=\"296\" y=\"306\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">No</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"340\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Synopsis 2026 to 2028, page 13 (99%).</text></svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Grouse, ptarmigan, turkey: yes. Quail, pheasant: no <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Hare, coyote, raccoon, skunk: yes <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Deer and ducks: never with a .22 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the methods table and notes</summary><ul><li>Page 13 methods table, rimfire column: upland game birds \"Yes, note 2\"; note 2 says \"Grouse, ptarmigan, or turkey only\" (99%, via <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods\">Rule Book: legal methods</a>).</li><li>\"Other small game (includes coyote)\": rimfire Yes <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Deer, black bear, elk, moose, sheep, goat, caribou, cougar, wolf: rimfire No <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Rimfire is legal for bobcat, lynx and wolverine among big game <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Migratory game birds (ducks, geese): rimfire No; shotgun or class D bow only <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Small game means \"fox, raccoon, coyote, skunk, snowshoe hare and game birds\" (99%, synopsis page 4, via <a href=\"#/s/rb-definitions\">definitions</a>).</li></ul></details>","<aside class=\"callout warn\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>You need</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Hunting licence</td><td>Page 8 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></td></tr><tr><td>No species licence for small game</td><td>Page 8 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Mission city limits or MU 2-4: Fraser Valley Special Area licence and $1,000,000 insurance</td><td>Pages 8 and 29 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></td></tr><tr><td><button class=\"term\" data-term=\"PAL\">PAL</button> (Possession and Acquisition Licence) to own the rifle</td><td>Firearms Act <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more on licences</summary><ul><li>Details and fees: <a href=\"#/s/rb-licences-fees\">Rule Book: licences and fees</a> and <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-2\">Region 2</a>.</li><li>Mission is in <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"MU\">MU</button> (Management Unit) 2-8; neighbours 2-4, 2-3 and 2-19 (90%, page 26 map, my reading in the Region 2 lesson).</li><li>PAL: a federal licence to own and buy firearms (95%, glossary). Whether a PAL is needed to buy .22 ammunition: <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> with the RCMP (Royal Canadian Mounted Police) Canadian Firearms Program.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 328\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Region 2 small game seasons a .22 can be used for, synopsis page 28: grouse September 10 to December 15; ptarmigan September 10 to December 15, not in MU 2-4; snowshoe hare August 1 to April 30 in MUs 2-5 to 2-19 only; coyote September 10 to June 15; raccoon and skunk September 1 to March 31. Grouse and ptarmigan also have a bow only season September 1 to 9.\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"328\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"27\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Region 2: small game seasons</text><line x1=\"140.0\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"140.0\" y2=\"258\" stroke=\"#D9E0D5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"151.0\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#17201A\">A</text><line x1=\"160.66666666666666\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"160.66666666666666\" y2=\"258\" stroke=\"#D9E0D5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"171.66666666666666\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#17201A\">S</text><line x1=\"181.33333333333334\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"181.33333333333334\" y2=\"258\" stroke=\"#D9E0D5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"192.33333333333334\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#17201A\">O</text><line x1=\"202.0\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"202.0\" y2=\"258\" stroke=\"#D9E0D5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"213.0\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#17201A\">N</text><line x1=\"222.66666666666669\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"222.66666666666669\" y2=\"258\" stroke=\"#D9E0D5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"233.66666666666669\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#17201A\">D</text><line x1=\"243.33333333333331\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"243.33333333333331\" y2=\"258\" stroke=\"#D9E0D5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"254.33333333333331\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#17201A\">J</text><line x1=\"264.0\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"264.0\" y2=\"258\" stroke=\"#D9E0D5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"275.0\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#17201A\">F</text><line x1=\"284.66666666666663\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"284.66666666666663\" y2=\"258\" stroke=\"#D9E0D5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"295.66666666666663\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#17201A\">M</text><line x1=\"305.33333333333337\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"305.33333333333337\" y2=\"258\" stroke=\"#D9E0D5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"316.33333333333337\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#17201A\">A</text><line x1=\"326.0\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"326.0\" y2=\"258\" stroke=\"#D9E0D5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"337.0\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#17201A\">M</text><line x1=\"346.66666666666663\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"346.66666666666663\" y2=\"258\" stroke=\"#D9E0D5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"357.66666666666663\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#17201A\">J</text><line x1=\"367.33333333333337\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"367.33333333333337\" y2=\"258\" stroke=\"#D9E0D5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"378.33333333333337\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#17201A\">J</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"76\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Grouse</text><rect x=\"166.8\" y=\"62\" width=\"65.4\" height=\"18\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"144\" y=\"96\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Sep 10 to Dec 15</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Ptarmigan*</text><rect x=\"166.8\" y=\"102\" width=\"65.4\" height=\"18\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"144\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Sep 10 to Dec 15</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"156\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Snowshoe hare*</text><rect x=\"140.0\" y=\"142\" width=\"185.0\" height=\"18\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"144\" y=\"176\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Aug 1 to Apr 30</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Coyote</text><rect x=\"166.8\" y=\"182\" width=\"189.4\" height=\"18\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"144\" y=\"216\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Sep 10 to Jun 15</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Raccoon, skunk</text><rect x=\"160.7\" y=\"222\" width=\"144.3\" height=\"18\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"144\" y=\"256\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Sep 1 to Mar 31</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"296\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">* Ptarmigan: not 2-4. Hare: 2-5 to 2-19 only.</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"316\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Region 2, page 28 (99%). Bow only Sep 1 to 9.</text></svg>\n</figure><aside class=\"callout warn\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside><ul><li>Grouse: Sept 10 to Dec 15, 10 a day, 30 in possession <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Snowshoe hare: Aug 1 to Apr 30, MUs 2-5 to 2-19, 10 a day <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul>","<div class=\"hm-seasons\" data-region=\"2\" data-mus=\"2-8,2-4,2-3,2-19\" data-species=\"grouse|ptarmigan|hare|coyote|raccoon|skunk\"><p class=\"hm-law\">Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p><p class=\"muted\">Season table loading...</p></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every row, page 28</summary><ul><li>Grouse, sooty (blue), ruffed and spruce together: Sept 10 to Dec 15 in 2-2 to 2-19; bow only Sept 1 to 9; 10 a day, 30 in possession (99%, page 28).</li><li>Ptarmigan: Sept 10 to Dec 15 in 2-2, 2-3, 2-5 to 2-19; not 2-4; 5 a day, 15 in possession <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Snowshoe hare: Aug 1 to Apr 30 in 2-5 to 2-19, 10 a day. No season in 2-2, 2-3 or 2-4 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Coyote: Sept 10 to June 15 in 2-2 to 2-19, no bag limit <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Raccoon, skunk: Sept 1 to Mar 31 in 2-2 to 2-19, no bag limit <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Turkey: no Region 2 row on page 28 (99%, Region 2 lesson). So no turkey with the .22 here.</li><li>Mission is MU 2-8, so all five are open there in season (99%, my reading of the rows above).</li></ul></details>","<aside class=\"callout warn\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Rule</th><th>Plain English</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Hours</td><td>1 hour before sunrise to 1 hour after sunset <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Bullets</td><td>No full metal jacket non expanding bullets <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Grouse meat</td><td>Both breasts go home <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the rules in full</summary><ul><li>Item 38, page 11: no hunting game, except migratory birds, from one hour after sunset to one hour before sunrise (99%, <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods\">legal methods</a>).</li><li>Page 12: \"It is unlawful to hunt or trap with a rifle using a full metal jacketed non-expanding bullet\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Most .22 LR hunting loads are lead or copper plated lead round nose or hollow point, not full metal jacket (80%, maker product pages). Read the box (Tip).</li><li>Edible portion of a game bird: both breasts go home (99%, <a href=\"#/s/rb-unlawful-acts\">Rule Book: unlawful acts</a>).</li><li>No light to hunt by, no infrared optics on the trip (99%, page 11).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 324\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Three rules that stop a .22 near Mission. Shot only areas, such as within 150 m of Highway 7 east of Mission, allow a shotgun only, no rifle. No shooting areas such as Map B12 Buntzen Lake allow no discharge at all. In or on any vehicle the chamber and the magazine must be empty; a magazine in the rifle counts as loaded.\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"324\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"27\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Where the .22 must stay quiet</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"44\" width=\"376\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"28\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#FF6A13\">Shot only area</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Shotgun only. No .22, no rifle.</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Hwy 7 east of Mission: 150 m</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"128\" width=\"376\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"28\" y=\"154\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">No shooting area</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">No firearm discharge at all.</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Map B12 Buntzen Lake and more</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"212\" width=\"376\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"28\" y=\"238\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Any vehicle</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Chamber AND magazine empty.</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Mag in the rifle = loaded</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"312\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Region 2 page 27, Closed Areas Regulation (99%).</text></svg>\n</figure><aside class=\"callout warn\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside><ul><li>Shot only areas: shotgun, not your .22 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>No shooting areas: no discharge at all <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: around Mission and Harrison</summary><ul><li>Highway 7, east of Mission to Highway 1: shot only within 150 m (99%, Closed Areas Regulation via <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-2\">Region 2</a>).</li><li>More shot only and no shooting land at Nicomen and Hatzic; Map B12 Buntzen Lake (2-8) is No Shooting; in 2-19, Maps B29 Elbow Lake, B32 Hemlock Valley, B33 Chehalis <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Fraser Valley Regional District roads: no discharge within 400 m unless lawfully hunting or trapping; target shooting is out (99%, page 27).</li><li>Harrison Hot Springs village: no firearm discharge anywhere inside the village, and no hunting exception (99%, Bylaw No. 1207, 2024, s. 3, via <a href=\"#/s/local-harrison-deer\">Harrison deer</a>). Mission's own bylaw adds areas (99%, see <a href=\"#/s/local-mission\">Local plan: Mission</a>).</li><li>Vehicles: chamber and magazine empty (99%, item 28).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 320\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Two pictures. Left: a grouse up in a tree with only sky behind it; the bullet keeps going, a .22 can carry over a kilometre, so no shot. Right: a grouse on the ground on a slope with earth behind; the bullet stops in the dirt, so the shot can be safe.\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"320\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"27\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Earth behind every shot</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"44\" width=\"184\" height=\"200\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#CFE3EE\"/><rect x=\"204\" y=\"44\" width=\"184\" height=\"200\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#CFE3EE\"/><path d=\"M204 150 Q300 120 388 160 L388 244 L204 244 Z\" fill=\"#7A6A4F\"/><path d=\"M12 210 L196 210 L196 244 L12 244 Z\" fill=\"#7A6A4F\"/><rect x=\"57\" y=\"110\" width=\"6\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#6E4A2A\"/><path d=\"M34 150 L60 70 L86 150 Z\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><rect x=\"147\" y=\"110\" width=\"6\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#6E4A2A\"/><path d=\"M124 150 L150 70 L176 150 Z\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><ellipse cx=\"150\" cy=\"96\" rx=\"10\" ry=\"7\" fill=\"#9A6B3F\"/><ellipse cx=\"300\" cy=\"150\" rx=\"11\" ry=\"7\" fill=\"#9A6B3F\"/><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"230\" x2=\"139.1\" y2=\"106.6\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M146 98 L134.4 102.8 L143.8 110.3z\" fill=\"#FF6A13\"/><line x1=\"156\" y1=\"92\" x2=\"196\" y2=\"60\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/><line x1=\"240\" y1=\"236\" x2=\"286.1\" y2=\"163.3\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M292 154 L281.0 160.1 L291.2 166.5z\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"104\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FF6A13\">NO: sky behind</text><text x=\"296\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">YES: earth behind</text><text x=\"104\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#17201A\">A .22 can carry</text><text x=\"104\" y=\"308\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#17201A\">over 1 km (65%)</text><text x=\"296\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#17201A\">Bullet stops in</text><text x=\"296\" y=\"308\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#17201A\">the dirt</text></svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Earth behind every shot (Tip; CZ rule 15, 95%).</li><li>Grouse: head or upper neck (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the shot in full</summary><ul><li>A .22 can travel well past 1 km <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>. CZ: \"several hundred meters\" past the target <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Never at water or rock (95%, CZ rule 16).</li><li>Grouse, hare: inside about 40 m from a rest (Tip). See <a href=\"#/s/rimfire-22\">the .22 rimfire</a> and <a href=\"#/s/mc-grouse-09\">grouse: how to hunt</a>.</li><li>Unload before you walk to the bird (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 352\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"What a .22 rimfire may legally hunt in BC, from the methods table on page 13 of the synopsis: grouse and ptarmigan yes, wild turkey yes (note 2: grouse, ptarmigan or turkey only among birds), snowshoe hare yes, coyote, raccoon and skunk yes. Quail and pheasant no, ducks and geese no, deer, bear, elk and moose no.\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"352\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"27\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">What the .22 may hunt in BC</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Rimfire (.22) in the page 13 methods table:</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"70\" width=\"372\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"91\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Grouse, ptarmigan</text><rect x=\"270\" y=\"75\" width=\"52\" height=\"20\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"296\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">Yes</text><text x=\"332\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">note 2</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"106\" width=\"372\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"127\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Wild turkey</text><rect x=\"270\" y=\"111\" width=\"52\" height=\"20\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"296\" y=\"126\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">Yes</text><text x=\"332\" y=\"126\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">note 2</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"142\" width=\"372\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"163\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Snowshoe hare</text><rect x=\"270\" y=\"147\" width=\"52\" height=\"20\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"296\" y=\"162\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">Yes</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"178\" width=\"372\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"199\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Coyote, raccoon, skunk</text><rect x=\"270\" y=\"183\" width=\"52\" height=\"20\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"296\" y=\"198\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">Yes</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"214\" width=\"372\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"235\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Quail, pheasant</text><rect x=\"270\" y=\"219\" width=\"52\" height=\"20\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#FF6A13\"/><text x=\"296\" y=\"234\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">No</text><text x=\"332\" y=\"234\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">note 2</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"250\" width=\"372\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"271\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Ducks, geese</text><rect x=\"270\" y=\"255\" width=\"52\" height=\"20\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#FF6A13\"/><text x=\"296\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">No</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"286\" width=\"372\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"307\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Deer, bear, elk, moose</text><rect x=\"270\" y=\"291\" width=\"52\" height=\"20\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#FF6A13\"/><text x=\"296\" y=\"306\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">No</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"340\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Synopsis 2026 to 2028, page 13 (99%).</text></svg>\n</figure><aside class=\"callout rule\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Grandpa's rule (wisdom): Know the bird, the season, the place and the backstop before the safety comes off.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout mistake\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Taking the .22 on a quail or duck trip. Shotgun only.</li><li>Hunting hare in MU 2-4 or 2-3: no hare season there.</li><li>Shooting from a road edge inside a shot only strip.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Before the walk: open the seasons block above for today and your MU. Screenshot it.</p></aside>","<ul><li>Synopsis 2026 to 2028, pages 3, 4, 8, 11 to 13, 26 to 29, via the Rule Book <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. CZ manual <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>. Checked 2026-10-23.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: all sources</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://www2.gov.bc.ca/assets/gov/sports-recreation-arts-and-culture/outdoor-recreation/fishing-and-hunting/hunting/regulations/hunting-trapping-synopsis.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BC Hunting and Trapping Regulations Synopsis 2026 to 2028, 2 October 2026 edition (PDF)</a>, as carried in the Rule Book sessions <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods\">legal methods</a>, <a href=\"#/s/rb-definitions\">definitions</a>, <a href=\"#/s/rb-unlawful-acts\">unlawful acts</a>, <a href=\"#/s/rb-licences-fees\">licences</a> and <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-2\">Region 2</a> (99%, checked there 2026-10-03 to 2026-10-04; restated here 2026-10-23).</li><li>Closed Areas Regulation lines via the Region 2 lesson (99% rule, 85% boundary reading).</li><li><a href=\"https://czubpimstorage.blob.core.windows.net/strapi-pim/assets/735342000443_CZ_457_05_2025_en_es_cs_de_fr_8dc25ceb9d.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CZ 457 instruction manual, 05 2025 (PDF)</a>: rules 15 and 16 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>.22 travel distance: <a href=\"#/s/rimfire-22\">the .22 rimfire</a> <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul></details>"]